</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Additional Experiments</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present additional results on the accuracy gap shown in Fig. <a href="#S5.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 5.2 Classification Results ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Multi-Class Support Vector Machine with Differential Privacy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> for the remaining datasets.
Fig. <a href="#A3.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ C.2 Additional Experiments ‣ Appendix C Experiments ‣ Multi-Class Support Vector Machine with Differential Privacy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> reports the results for weight-perturbation methods, and Fig. <a href="#A3.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ C.2 Additional Experiments ‣ Appendix C Experiments ‣ Multi-Class Support Vector Machine with Differential Privacy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> shows the results for gradient-perturbation methods.
We present additional results on the convergence shown in Fig. <a href="#S5.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Convergence ‣ 5.3 Additional Experiments ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Multi-Class Support Vector Machine with Differential Privacy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> for the remaining datasets in
Fig. <a href="#A3.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ C.2 Additional Experiments ‣ Appendix C Experiments ‣ Multi-Class Support Vector Machine with Differential Privacy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
